Matelot Customer Licence Agreement (EULA)
Version 0.1 — draft, pending legal review

Matelot (the "Software") — the container images, Helm charts, command-line tools and documentation published by
Matelot ("we", "us") — is proprietary software. It is licensed, not sold.

1. Licence. Subject to this agreement and to an active subscription (or the Free tier where offered), we grant you
   a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and run the Software on infrastructure you
   control, for your organization's internal business purposes, for the number of users your subscription covers.

2. Restrictions. You may not: (a) sell, rent, lease, sublicense, host for third parties or otherwise provide the
   Software as a service to anyone outside your organization, except as expressly permitted by an MSSP or reseller
   agreement with us; (b) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, or attempt to derive its source
   code, except to the extent applicable law expressly permits; (c) remove or alter any proprietary notice;
   (d) circumvent licence, user-count or feature restrictions; (e) publish benchmarks of the Software without our
   consent.

3. Your data. Everything the Software processes stays on your infrastructure. We do not access your data unless you
   send it to us (for example in a support request), and then only to provide support.

4. Third-party components. The Software contains open-source components under their own licences, listed in the SBOM
   published with every release. Those licences apply to those components.

5. Updates and support. Releases, release notes and security advisories are published on GitHub. Support is provided
   according to your subscription tier (see SUPPORT.md).

6. Warranty disclaimer. THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING
   MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT, TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW.

7. Limitation of liability. TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, WE ARE NOT LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL OR
   CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES, AND OUR TOTAL LIABILITY UNDER THIS AGREEMENT IS LIMITED TO THE FEES YOU PAID FOR THE
   SOFTWARE IN THE TWELVE MONTHS BEFORE THE CLAIM.

8. Term and termination. This agreement lasts as long as your subscription. It terminates automatically if you breach
   it; on termination you stop using the Software and delete the images and charts. Sections 3, 4, 6, 7 and 9 survive.

9. General. This agreement is governed by the laws of the country in which Matelot is established, excluding its
   conflict-of-law rules; the courts of that country have exclusive jurisdiction. If a provision is unenforceable,
   the rest remains in force. This is the entire agreement between you and us about the Software, unless you have a
   separately signed agreement with us, which prevails.

Contact: sales@matelot.io · security@matelot.io
